  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "title": "Due Course",
  "dates": "Monday, November 9 – Thursday, November 19, 2009",
  "logline": "A bill comes due, home calls at one in the morning, somebody stays to the end of a song — and Christmas comes up early.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "On the Portolá steps Becca asked if she could tell her mom you’re her boyfriend. You said yes, and meant to mean it.",
      "if": "e14_ask==\"weight\""
    },
    {
      "text": "At Sully’s you told Becca you’re going to ask Lena home for Thanksgiving. She zipped her lips: “It’s yours to ask. I’m not *allowed*.”",
      "if": "becca_knows_lena_ask"
    },
    {
      "text": "Walking home at one in the morning, Lena said she’d go anywhere on the twenty-sixth where nobody knows his name. You took her to Lupe’s — and decided to ask her to Youngstown, properly, in a week.",
      "if": "e14_invite==\"lupes\" && jack_plans_ask_lena"
    },
    {
      "text": "Your mother, about Becca: “Then Christmas! Bring her at Christmas. I’ll make the cardoons.” You told her a friend from school might come for Thanksgiving. Lena.",
      "if": "maria_wants_becca_xmas && maria_knows_lena_maybe"
    },
    {
      "text": "Julian asked Lena to Bastille on Thursday to hear his new song. You said you’d be there — to the end.",
      "if": "lena_julian_bastille"
    },
    {
      "text": "“Ask me again in a week. —L.”"
    }
  ],
